{"step_index":1082,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:41:20Z","input_tokens":2111,"cache_read_tokens":207279,"output_tokens":2595,"thinking":"The code aims to clean numeric fields by removing commas and ensuring proper parsing. It iterates through a list of keys, retrieving their values from the data. The code checks if the value exists, is not empty, and is not \"null\", before parsing the value using a specific function. This function ensures clean conversion of the value to a number.\n\n\nCalculated subtotal is derived from cleaned item data. A grand total sanity check will compare the calculated subtotal plus total tax against the extracted grand total. If a total is detected in words, the value will be extracted for validation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py","Replacement":"    # 3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly via parse_inr\n    for key in [\"subtotal\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"declared_total\"]:\n        val = data.get(key)\n        if val is not None and str(val).strip() != \"\" and str(val).lower() != \"null\":\n            data[key] = parse_inr(val)\n\n    # 4. SUB-TOTAL CALCULATION:\n    # Do not trust random OCR numbers near bank details for Subtotal.\n    # Calculate the Subtotal deterministically from the extracted items:\n    # subtotal = sum(item.quantity * item.unit_rate for item in items)\n    if clean_items:\n        calculated_subtotal = round(sum(it[\"quantity\"] * it[\"unit_rate\"] for it in clean_items), 2)\n        data[\"subtotal\"] = calculated_subtotal\n        data[\"calculated_subtotal\"] = calculated_subtotal\n    else:\n        calculated_subtotal = float(data.get(\"subtotal\") or 0.0)\n\n    # 5. GRAND TOTAL SANITY CHECK:\n    # Grand Total must be approximately (Subtotal + Total Tax).\n    # If the OCR extracted '774' or '585132', reject them because they are bank/account/IFSC digits.\n    cgst = float(data.get(\"cgst\") or 0.0)\n    sgst = float(data.get(\"sgst\") or 0.0)\n    igst = float(data.get(\"igst\") or 0.0)\n    total_tax = round(cgst + sgst + igst, 2)\n    expected_total = round(calculated_subtotal + total_tax, 2)\n\n    # Check for printed Grand Total in Words line (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY')\n    word_total = 0.0\n    raw_ocr = str(data.get(\"raw_ocr_text\") or data.get(\"raw_text\") or data.get(\"notes\") or \"\")\n    for candidate_text in [raw_ocr, str(data.get(\"notes\") or \"\"), str(data.get(\"amount_in_words\") or \"\"), str(data.get(\"total_in_words\") or \"\")]:\n        if candidate_text:\n            for line in candidate_text.splitlines():\n                if re.search(r'(?:total|amount|rupees)\\s+(?:in\\s+words|in\\s+word)', line, re.IGNORECASE) or re.search(r'rupees\\s+[a-zA-Z\\s]+only', line, re.IGNORECASE):\n                    wt = parse_words_to_number(line)\n                    if wt > 0:\n                        word_total = wt\n                        break\n        if word_total > 0:\n            break\n\n    current_declared = float(data.get(\"declared_total\") or 0.0)\n    \n    # Reject bank/account/IFSC digits (e.g. 774, 585132) if wildly outside expected total\n    is_declared_suspicious = False\n    if expected_total > 0:\n        if current_declared <= 0:\n            is_declared_suspicious = True\n        elif current_declared < (expected_total * 0.70) or current_declared > (expected_total * 1.50):\n            is_declared_suspicious = True\n\n    if word_total > 0:\n        # Cross-check against printed words confirms grand total\n        data[\"declared_total\"] = word_total\n        data[\"total_declared\"] = word_total\n    elif is_declared_suspicious and expected_total > 0:\n        final_total = round(expected_total) if abs(expected_total - round(expected_total)) < 0.20 else expected_total\n        data[\"declared_total\"] = final_total\n        data[\"total_declared\"] = final_total\n    else:\n        data[\"total_declared\"] = current_declared if current_declared > 0 else expected_total\n        data[\"declared_total\"] = data[\"total_declared\"]\n\n    # Ensure schema aliases for frontend compatibility\n    if data.get(\"invoice_number\") and not data.get(\"invoice_no\"):\n        data[\"invoice_no\"] = data[\"invoice_number\"]\n\n    return data","Target":"    # 3. Ensure numeric fields strip commas cleanly via parse_inr\n    for key in [\"subtotal\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"declared_total\"]:\n        val = data.get(key)\n        if val is not None and str(val).strip() != \"\" and str(val).lower() != \"null\":\n            data[key] = parse_inr(val)\n\n    # 4. Check for printed Grand Total in Words to correct OCR misreads (e.g. 2173.9 -> 4490.0)\n    raw_ocr = str(data.get(\"raw_ocr_text\") or data.get(\"raw_text\") or data.get(\"notes\") or \"\")\n    if raw_ocr:\n        for line in raw_ocr.splitlines():\n            if re.search(r'(?:total|amount|rupees)\\s+(?:in\\s+words|in\\s+word)', line, re.IGNORECASE) or re.search(r'rupees\\s+[a-zA-Z\\s]+only', line, re.IGNORECASE):\n                word_total = parse_words_to_number(line)\n                if word_total > 0:\n                    current_declared = data.get(\"declared_total\") or 0.0\n                    if current_declared == 0.0 or abs(current_declared - word_total) > 10:\n                        data[\"declared_total\"] = word_total\n                    break\n\n    # Ensure schema aliases for frontend compatibility\n    if data.get(\"declared_total\") is not None:\n        data[\"total_declared\"] = data[\"declared_total\"]\n    elif data.get(\"total_declared\") is not None:\n        data[\"declared_total\"] = data[\"total_declared\"]\n\n    if data.get(\"invoice_number\") and not data.get(\"invoice_no\"):\n        data[\"invoice_no\"] = data[\"invoice_number\"]\n\n    return data"}}]}
