{"step_index":1089,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:42:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T00:12:04+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T00:12:04+05:30\nShowing lines 10-50 of 283\n10: const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are an Indian GST Tax Invoice extractor. Your job is to extract exact numbers and text without dropping digits or inventing items.\n11: \n12: CRITICAL RULES:\n13: 1. COMMA & NUMBER HANDLING (DO NOT DROP DIGITS):\n14:    - In Indian currency notation, commas are thousands separators. NEVER drop digits before commas!\n15:    - Example: '2,535.00' is 2535.0 (Two Thousand Five Hundred Thirty-Five), NOT 535.\n16:    - Example: '1,270.00' is 1270.0 (One Thousand Two Hundred Seventy), NOT 270.\n17:    - Always verify extracted figures against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n18: \n19: NUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\n20: - Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\n21: - If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n22: - All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \"2,535.00\", \"1\", \"4,490.00\").\n23: \n24: 2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n25:    - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n26:    - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n27:    - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n28: \n29: 3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n30:    - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n31:    - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n32: \n33: 4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n34:    - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n35:    - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n36:    - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\n37: \n38: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n39: {\n40:   \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n41:   \"gstin\": string or null,\n42:   \"invoice_number\": string or null,\n43:   \"date\": string or null,\n44:   \"items\": [\n45:     {\n46:       \"description\": string,\n47:       \"quantity\": string,\n48:       \"unit_rate\": string,\n49:       \"total_amount\": string\n50:     }"}
{"step_index":1090,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:42:04Z","input_tokens":2618,"cache_read_tokens":213977,"output_tokens":1184,"tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js","Replacement":"const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are a strict GST Invoice extractor. \nRULES FOR LINE ITEMS:\n- Extract items ONLY from the central itemized table bounded between the table header (S.No, Description, HSN, Qty, Rate, Amount) and the Subtotal row.\n- NEVER extract text from the header or footer as line items:\n  * DO NOT extract addresses or cities (e.g. 'Mumbai, Maharashtra').\n  * DO NOT extract PAN, GSTIN, or buyer details (e.g. 'PAN : 26CORPP').\n  * DO NOT extract bank account or payment details (e.g. 'Acc. Number 271').\n- Each valid line item MUST have a legitimate product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and total amount.\n\nGRAND TOTAL:\n- Extract the final payable Grand Total printed at the bottom of the bill (e.g., '4,490.00' / 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY'). Do NOT extract partial account numbers or phone numbers as the grand total.\n\nNUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\n- If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n- All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \"2,535.00\", \"1\", \"4,490.00\").\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:","Target":"const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `You are an Indian GST Tax Invoice extractor. Your job is to extract exact numbers and text without dropping digits or inventing items.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. COMMA & NUMBER HANDLING (DO NOT DROP DIGITS):\n   - In Indian currency notation, commas are thousands separators. NEVER drop digits before commas!\n   - Example: '2,535.00' is 2535.0 (Two Thousand Five Hundred Thirty-Five), NOT 535.\n   - Example: '1,270.00' is 1270.0 (One Thousand Two Hundred Seventy), NOT 270.\n   - Always verify extracted figures against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n\nNUMERIC INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Never discard digits before commas! '2,535.00' must be extracted as '2,535.00'. '1,270.00' must be extracted as '1,270.00'. '4,490.00' must be extracted as '4,490.00'.\n- If you are unsure about the digits before the comma, read the 'Amount in Words' printed on the bill (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY') to confirm the thousands digit.\n- All numbers and rates must be extracted as strings (e.g. \"2,535.00\", \"1\", \"4,490.00\").\n\n2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n   - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n   - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n   - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n\n3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n   - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n   - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n\n4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n   - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n   - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n   - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:"}}]}
